        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Suppose that we want to evaluate the integral</p>",
            "readable_text": "Suppose that we want to evaluate the integral",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\int x\\ln{x}\\, \\textrm{d}x \\,.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\int x\\ln{x}\\, \\textrm{d}x \\,.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The method of integration by parts can help us solve this problem. Let&#x27;s remind ourselves of the &quot;by-parts&quot; formula,\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\int u v&#x27; \\textrm{d}x = uv - \\int v u&#x27;\\textrm{d}x.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "The method of integration by parts can help us solve this problem. Let's remind ourselves of the \"by-parts\" formula,\n[MATH: \\int u v' \\textrm{d}x = uv - \\int v u'\\textrm{d}x.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We usually let <span class=\"math\">[MATH: u = x,]</span> but that would leave us with <span class=\"math\">[MATH: v&#x27; = \\ln(x)]</span> which is hard to integrate. So instead, we&#x27;re going to choose our <span class=\"math\">[MATH: u]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: v&#x27;]</span> slightly differently, as follows:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: u = \\ln x|\u27f9u^{\u2032} = (1)/(x); v^{\u2032} = x|\u27f9v = (1)/(2)x^{2}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We usually let [MATH: u = x,] but that would leave us with [MATH: v' = \\ln(x)] which is hard to integrate. So instead, we're going to choose our [MATH: u] and [MATH: v'] slightly differently, as follows:\n[MATH: u = \\ln x|\u27f9u^{\u2032} = (1)/(x); v^{\u2032} = x|\u27f9v = (1)/(2)x^{2}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Now the formula of integration by parts gives</p>",
            "readable_text": "Now the formula of integration by parts gives",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u222bx\\ln xdx|= \u222b\\ln x_(\u23df)_(u) \u22c5 x_(\u23df)_(v^{\u2032})dx; = \\ln x \u22c5 (1)/(2)x^{2} \u2212 \u222b(1)/(2)x^{2} \u22c5 (1)/(x)dx; = (1)/(2)x^{2}\\ln x \u2212 (1)/(2)\u222bxdx; = (1)/(2)x^{2}\\ln x \u2212 (1)/(4)x^{2} + C.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \u222bx\\ln xdx|= \u222b\\ln x_(\u23df)_(u) \u22c5 x_(\u23df)_(v^{\u2032})dx; = \\ln x \u22c5 (1)/(2)x^{2} \u2212 \u222b(1)/(2)x^{2} \u22c5 (1)/(x)dx; = (1)/(2)x^{2}\\ln x \u2212 (1)/(2)\u222bxdx; = (1)/(2)x^{2}\\ln x \u2212 (1)/(4)x^{2} + C.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>When we apply integration by parts to integrals containing logarithmic functions, we should <em>always</em> identify the logarithmic function with <span class=\"math\">[MATH: u,]</span> not with <span class=\"math\">[MATH: v&#x27;.]</span> </p>",
            "readable_text": "When we apply integration by parts to integrals containing logarithmic functions, we should always identify the logarithmic function with [MATH: u,] not with [MATH: v'.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nSuppose that we want to evaluate the integral\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\int x\\ln{x}\\, \\textrm{d}x \\,.]\n\nContent:\nThe method of integration by parts can help us solve this problem. Let's remind ourselves of the \"by-parts\" formula,\n[MATH: \\int u v' \\textrm{d}x = uv - \\int v u'\\textrm{d}x.]\n\nContent:\nWe usually let [MATH: u = x,] but that would leave us with [MATH: v' = \\ln(x)] which is hard to integrate. So instead, we're going to choose our [MATH: u] and [MATH: v'] slightly differently, as follows:\n[MATH: u = \\ln x|\u27f9u^{\u2032} = (1)/(x); v^{\u2032} = x|\u27f9v = (1)/(2)x^{2}.]\n\nContent:\nNow the formula of integration by parts gives\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \u222bx\\ln xdx|= \u222b\\ln x_(\u23df)_(u) \u22c5 x_(\u23df)_(v^{\u2032})dx; = \\ln x \u22c5 (1)/(2)x^{2} \u2212 \u222b(1)/(2)x^{2} \u22c5 (1)/(x)dx; = (1)/(2)x^{2}\\ln x \u2212 (1)/(2)\u222bxdx; = (1)/(2)x^{2}\\ln x \u2212 (1)/(4)x^{2} + C.]\n\nContent:\nWhen we apply integration by parts to integrals containing logarithmic functions, we should always identify the logarithmic function with [MATH: u,] not with [MATH: v'.]"
      },
