        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Evaluate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Evaluate [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining <span class=\"math\">[MATH: u]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: v&#x27;,]</span> as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: u = \\ln (x^{3})|\u27f9u^{\u2032} = (1)/(x^{3}) \u22c5 3x^{2} = (3)/(x); v^{\u2032} = 4x|\u27f9v = \u222b4xdx = 2x^{2}]</span></p><p>Using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u222b_{1}^{e}4x\\ln (x^{3})dx|= \u222b_{1}^{e}uv^{\u2032}dx; = uv|_{1}^{e} \u2212 \u222b_{1}^{e}vu^{\u2032}dx; = \\ln (x^{3}) \u22c5 (2x^{2})|_{1}^{e} \u2212 \u222b_{1}^{e}(2x^{2}) \u22c5 (3)/(x)dx; = [2(e)^{2}\\ln (e^{3}) \u2212 2(1)^{2}\\ln (1^{3})] \u2212 6\u222b_{1}^{e}xdx; = 6e^{2} \u2212 6((1)/(2)x^{2})|_{1}^{e}; = 6e^{2} \u2212 3x^{2}|_{1}^{e}; = 6e^{2} \u2212 3(e^{2} \u2212 1^{2}); = 3e^{2} + 3.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining [MATH: u] and [MATH: v',] as follows:\n\n[MATH: u = \\ln (x^{3})|\u27f9u^{\u2032} = (1)/(x^{3}) \u22c5 3x^{2} = (3)/(x); v^{\u2032} = 4x|\u27f9v = \u222b4xdx = 2x^{2}]\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n[MATH: \u222b_{1}^{e}4x\\ln (x^{3})dx|= \u222b_{1}^{e}uv^{\u2032}dx; = uv|_{1}^{e} \u2212 \u222b_{1}^{e}vu^{\u2032}dx; = \\ln (x^{3}) \u22c5 (2x^{2})|_{1}^{e} \u2212 \u222b_{1}^{e}(2x^{2}) \u22c5 (3)/(x)dx; = [2(e)^{2}\\ln (e^{3}) \u2212 2(1)^{2}\\ln (1^{3})] \u2212 6\u222b_{1}^{e}xdx; = 6e^{2} \u2212 6((1)/(2)x^{2})|_{1}^{e}; = 6e^{2} \u2212 3x^{2}|_{1}^{e}; = 6e^{2} \u2212 3(e^{2} \u2212 1^{2}); = 3e^{2} + 3.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining [MATH: u] and [MATH: v',] as follows:\n\n[MATH: u = \\ln (x^{3})|\u27f9u^{\u2032} = (1)/(x^{3}) \u22c5 3x^{2} = (3)/(x); v^{\u2032} = 4x|\u27f9v = \u222b4xdx = 2x^{2}]\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n[MATH: \u222b_{1}^{e}4x\\ln (x^{3})dx|= \u222b_{1}^{e}uv^{\u2032}dx; = uv|_{1}^{e} \u2212 \u222b_{1}^{e}vu^{\u2032}dx; = \\ln (x^{3}) \u22c5 (2x^{2})|_{1}^{e} \u2212 \u222b_{1}^{e}(2x^{2}) \u22c5 (3)/(x)dx; = [2(e)^{2}\\ln (e^{3}) \u2212 2(1)^{2}\\ln (1^{3})] \u2212 6\u222b_{1}^{e}xdx; = 6e^{2} \u2212 6((1)/(2)x^{2})|_{1}^{e}; = 6e^{2} \u2212 3x^{2}|_{1}^{e}; = 6e^{2} \u2212 3(e^{2} \u2212 1^{2}); = 3e^{2} + 3.]"
      },
