        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: \\displaystyle \\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nAt first, it may not look like we have two factors. Actually, we do, but one of them is implicit. The trick is to write the integral as\n[MATH: \\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\int \\ln{x} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\textrm{d}x.]\n\nUsing this trick, we can now use integration by parts. We let\n\n[MATH: u = \\ln x|\u27f9u^{\u2032} = (1)/(x); v^{\u2032} = 1|\u27f9v = x.]\n\nNow, using the by-parts formula, we get\n\n[MATH: \u222b\\ln xdx|= x\\ln x \u2212 \u222bx \u22c5 (1)/(x)dx; = x\\ln x \u2212 \u222b1dx; = x\\ln x \u2212 x + C; = x(\\ln x \u2212 1) + C.]"
